From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 23:12:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Block all control chars in PPD localization strings

Backport of upstream OpenPrinting/cups commit
989cfca122a4299bfca0f33ff6529c1710aba9e3 (branch 2.4.x line; first
target 2.4.17+, master also). ppd_put_string() previously stopped only at
LF when copying localized text into the PPD; other control characters
(CR, TAB, NUL, ESC...) were copied verbatim into the localization line.
Localized text can originate from the remote printer-strings-uri gettext
file fetched by _ppdCreateFromIPP2 (attacker-controlled HTTP content), so
reject ALL control characters (<0x20 and 0x7f) as the truncation
condition, matching upstream.

Upstream-commit: 989cfca122a4299bfca0f33ff6529c1710aba9e3
diff --git a/cups/ppd-cache.c b/cups/ppd-cache.c
index 9bffd54a..add58e3d 100644
--- a/cups/ppd-cache.c
+++ b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -5462,9 +5462,9 @@ ppd_put_string(cups_file_t  *fp,	/* I - PPD file */
       return;
   }
 
-  // Add the first line of localized text...
+    // Add the first line of localized text...
   cupsFilePrintf(fp, "*%s.%s %s/", lang->language, ppd_option, ppd_choice);
-  while (*text && *text != '\n')
+  while (*text && (*text & 255) >= ' ')
   {
     // Escape ":" and "<"...
     if (*text == ':' || *text == '<')
